WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:05.560
Robert Orlean, and his partner in crime, John
Streep, zipped through the murky waters of

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.559
the Louisiana Bayou on a speedboat.

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:13.900
These men were dealers in the illicit, but
their specialty was not any kind of contraband

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:19.880
you’d probably recognize: Orlean and Streep
dealt in rare orchids, illegally poached from

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:25.720
areas where they’re considered endangered,
and sold to high-paying rare plant collectors.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:31.910
As any seller or collector knows, rarity is
the hallmark of value, and what these two

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:35.612
men would encounter in the swamp that day
was truly one of a kind.

00:00:35.612 --> 00:00:41.910
The problem for this pair of greedy opportunists
is that only one of them would live to tell

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:47.350
the tale, and thanks to the SCP Foundation,
the other wouldn’t remember it for long.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:52.890
That’s what happens when you have a dangerous
run-in with a certain mean, green, swamp-dwelling

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.960
creature that doesn’t take kindly to unwanted
visitors.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.290
And no, we’re not talking about a crocodile.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:04.350
Orlean and Streep continued through the swamp,
keeping their keen eyes out for the flash

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:08.050
of light blue that’d give away the orchids
they were seeking.

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:14.100
Little did they know, from the murky darkness
between the reeds, a pair of big, yellow eyes

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.170
were watching them back.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:19.330
They were intruders in a stranger’s land.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.870
Threats, just like the Bad Man.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:27.390
They would need to be dealt with accordingly,
or a grim history would repeat itself.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:32.300
The boat came to a halt, as the two poachers
finally saw one of the rare flowers they were

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.180
looking for, arising out of the muck.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:38.580
Orlean leaped from the boat and began wading
towards his prize.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:42.470
The flower would fetch him and his partner
a pretty penny if they could get it back in

00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:43.470
good condition.

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:48.360
The motions were so well-practiced for Orlean,
so automatic, that he didn’t even notice

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.470
something was moving through the waters towards
him.

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:56.150
Gators and snakes were an occupational hazard
for people like Orlean - he kept a revolver

00:01:56.150 --> 00:02:01.610
holstered just below his shoulder as a precaution
- but the thing about to kill him was unlike

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:04.830
anything he’d ever faced before.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:09.450
Just as his careful fingers curled around
the orchid’s stem, Orlean heard Streep screaming

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.450
from the boat.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:15.720
He was frantically pointing at something just
beyond Orlean, emerging from the reeds.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:20.430
Orlean turned and felt his jaw falling open
in horror at the sight of it.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:23.640
At first, it seemed almost like a waterlogged
corpse.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:29.350
Thick, matted black hair, heavy with grease
and muddy bog water, teeming with parasitic

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:30.690
swamp-life.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:36.650
Her skin was green and bumpy, like that of
a toad, dripping with viscous, green sweat

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:39.870
that seemed like it could only be the by-product
of rot.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:48.870
But those eyes, those big, yellow amphibian
eyes, they were alive as they were inhuman.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:53.560
This creature wasn’t a corpse, it was something
else entirely.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:58.800
Her body cleared the water, standing at Orlean’s
height now and facing him, eye to eye.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:03.200
She was naked, her dignity preserved by her
long tangle of hair.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:08.190
Her body was human-shaped, except for her
freakishly long, thin limbs.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:14.410
Her belly appeared visibly bloated or engorged,
like a woman in the mid-stages of pregnancy.

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:19.970
Orlean had never smelled something so foul
in his entire life, which was mostly spent

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.410
wading through swamps and bogs.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.920
She smelled like death itself.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:29.090
Streep was screaming for Orlean to climb back
into the boat, but Orlean knew it was already

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:30.250
too late.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:34.380
He reached for his holstered pistol, but before
he could clear leather, the creature let out

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:40.790
a horrific, guttural hawking noise, and spewed
a stream of black goo onto Orlean’s face.

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:46.970
It was hot, sticky, and foul-tasting, like
a kind of tar rendered from corpses.

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:51.120
It plastered his open mouth and nose shut,
and began to suffocate him.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.700
He tried desperately to claw at his face and
tear the offending substance away, but all

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:59.050
that succeeded in doing was getting his fingers
stuck.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:04.100
While Orlean suffocated and Streep screamed
terrified obscenities from the boat, the creature

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:07.459
just watched and smiled through rotten teeth.

00:04:07.459 --> 00:04:12.660
It was nice to see them panic, just like the
Bad Man who’d come before.

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:14.330
They were in the wrong.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:16.569
They deserved this.

00:04:16.569 --> 00:04:20.039
Orlean soon realized that nothing he could
do would save himself.

00:04:20.039 --> 00:04:25.960
He’d spent his life in a dangerous profession,
and been lucky until now, but the reaper catches

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:28.090
up with everyone eventually.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:34.629
The last thing he saw as the world went black
was this creature - this Swamp Woman - wading

00:04:34.629 --> 00:04:38.490
towards him through the water with a hungry
look in her eye.

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:42.020
She grabbed him on either side of his face,
and just held him there.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:43.699
What was that sound?

00:04:43.699 --> 00:04:44.699
Was it fizzling?

00:04:44.699 --> 00:04:47.599
Like something was burning, or even melting?

00:04:47.599 --> 00:04:52.080
She just kept staring and smiling with those
awful rotten teeth.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:56.610
Robert Orlean went to sleep in her hands and
never woke up.

00:04:56.610 --> 00:05:00.229
Back on the boat, a desperate John Streep
was watching a scene that - if it wasn’t

00:05:00.229 --> 00:05:06.569
for the later intervention of the SCP Foundation
- would haunt him until his dying day.

00:05:06.569 --> 00:05:11.759
He watched his partner undergo a process that
was somewhere between rotting and melting.

00:05:11.759 --> 00:05:16.909
He withered away in the Swamp Woman’s hands,
degrading into thick, black sludge that she

00:05:16.909 --> 00:05:19.639
drank through her thirsty skin.

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:24.800
As much as it pained him to leave his friend
behind, Streep knew that there was no saving

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.039
him now.

00:05:26.039 --> 00:05:29.770
All he could possibly do was escape with his
own life.

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:34.659
He pulled the ripcord on the boat’s motor,
and tore his way back to the nearest township,

00:05:34.659 --> 00:05:39.169
the shape of the nightmarish Swamp Woman shrinking
in the distance behind him.

00:05:39.169 --> 00:05:44.529
When he ran into the local police station,
half-mad with grief and fear, screaming about

00:05:44.529 --> 00:05:48.930
the monster that killed his friend in the
swamp, the police understandably detained

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:50.870
him for further questioning.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:55.150
When his criminal history as a poacher was
flagged up on the database, it became clear

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:57.449
he probably wasn’t leaving for a while.

00:05:57.449 --> 00:06:02.699
That’s when a Foundation agent embedded
in the department passed a memo about the

00:06:02.699 --> 00:06:07.680
case’s strangeness up the chain of command,
and a covert Mobile Task Force was soon dispatched

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:12.300
to the swamp in order to locate and capture
the anomalous creature that Streep had claimed

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.460
took his friend’s life..

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:19.930
After a few days of searching, the Swamp Woman
was captured by the Foundation and redesignated

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:25.539
as SCP-811, before being delivered back to
a nearby containment site.

00:06:25.539 --> 00:06:30.240
Luckily for Foundation disinformation agents,
the cover story was practically gift-wrapped

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:35.400
for them on this one: It had been a dispute
between two hardcore criminals, and as the

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:39.589
saying goes, there’s no honor among thieves.

00:06:39.589 --> 00:06:44.520
Streep had murdered Orlean over a pay cut
dispute, and thrown him into the swamp, where

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.949
his body was eaten by gators.

00:06:46.949 --> 00:06:51.900
A few falsified records and implanted memories
later, and the Foundation was free to do what

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:53.960
it pleased with SCP-811.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:59.789
But the Swamp Woman would prove to be full
of surprises and contradictions.

00:06:59.789 --> 00:07:05.800
While designated Euclid, the containment procedures
for the creature were rather extensive - for

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:07.559
its own benefit.

00:07:07.559 --> 00:07:11.939
Like a lot of creatures who’d never existed
in captivity before, it had very specific

00:07:11.939 --> 00:07:17.249
needs in terms of its artificial habitat - the
Foundation needed to be on top of everything

00:07:17.249 --> 00:07:22.520
from the pH levels of its soil acidity to
the optimal temperatures and humidity levels

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:27.729
of its containment chamber, built to resemble
the creature’s natural swamp habitat.

00:07:27.729 --> 00:07:32.889
The Swamp Woman is mostly non-aggressive to
Foundation staff, but certain precautions

00:07:32.889 --> 00:07:36.599
need to be taken in order to ensure everyone’s
safety around her.

00:07:36.599 --> 00:07:42.300
While she’s largely humanoid, her internal
physiology vastly differs from that of humans.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:45.569
Her veins and digestive system are non-functional.

00:07:45.569 --> 00:07:50.119
She consumes her prey by melting it into black
sludge with the highly caustic secretions

00:07:50.119 --> 00:07:53.999
of her skin, before absorbing it back through
her pores.

00:07:53.999 --> 00:07:57.969
The waste material collects in her stomach,
which she then expels voluntarily through

00:07:57.969 --> 00:08:00.389
an action similar to vomiting.

00:08:00.389 --> 00:08:06.389
This is often used defensively, or in hunting
prey, as the unfortunate Robert Orlean found

00:08:06.389 --> 00:08:07.389
out.

00:08:07.389 --> 00:08:12.569
As a result, people working in 811’s containment
chamber need to do so in pairs and wear heavily

00:08:12.569 --> 00:08:16.080
sealed hazmat suits for obvious safety reasons.

00:08:16.080 --> 00:08:18.930
The creature also proved to be surprisingly
intelligent.

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:25.020
While not a genius by any means, it was no
mere mindless animal: the Swamp Woman had

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:30.189
an intellect and communication skills on par
with your average feral child, though one

00:08:30.189 --> 00:08:34.930
that had been brought up and socialized in
a relatively normal home before being turned

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:39.900
loose and experiencing a decline in its mental
and social development.

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:45.040
Her words have a childlike construction to
them, as though English isn’t her native

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:48.960
language, and she’s still in the very early
stages of learning it.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:54.381
She gave herself a name, “Aé”, and began
to cooperate well with Foundation staff, in

00:08:54.381 --> 00:08:56.960
exchange for having her needs met.

00:08:56.960 --> 00:09:01.470
Since being brought into containment, she’s
made a number of requests: These included

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:05.760
some requests that had been denied by the
Foundation, such as the regular provision

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:10.570
of bovine prey for its chamber and a variety
of fish from its native environment to make

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:12.300
it feel more at home.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:17.410
However, there are some requests that the
Foundation has approved, like a wooden hairbrush,

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:23.050
and a D-Class in a hazmat suit entering the
room daily in order to help wash her hair,

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:28.440
often bogged down by the frequency at which
her skin produces thick, caustic oils.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:33.660
In one particularly strange request, she asked
for a turtle in a hazmat suit to act as a

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:38.970
companion in her containment chamber, as she
reacted negatively to the idea of having turtles

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.010
as food.

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:43.490
Sadly, this was one of the denied requests.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:50.750
SCP-811 was also involved in a few cross-tests
with other anomalies, leading to curious results.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:56.000
After realizing just how dangerous SCP-811’s
secretions could be, Foundation researchers

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:02.450
naturally floated the idea of using it on
SCP-682, in its seemingly endless termination

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:03.450
experiments.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:08.510
A sample of 682’s flesh was successfully
decayed by the dangerous mucus, so a larger

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:12.830
quantity, collected over a number of months,
was then sprayed all over the beast.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:18.890
It managed to reduce 682’s body mass by
27%, melting its way through the covered flesh

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:20.240
down to the bone.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:26.500
However, at that point, it was unable to decay
further, and SCP-682 soon returned back to

00:10:26.500 --> 00:10:27.980
its normal state.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.690
Who could have possibly seen that coming,
right?

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:37.990
However, a much more interesting and enlightening
cross-test occurred with SCP-978, the Desire

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:39.080
Camera.

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:42.880
If you haven’t already seen our video on
the Desire Camera, it’s pretty much exactly

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:48.200
what the name suggests: A polaroid camera
that reveals the deepest desire of its subject,

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:53.470
and the Foundation decided to test it on a
large number of staff and anomalies - one

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:55.110
of those being SCP-811.

00:10:55.110 --> 00:11:01.570
When a photograph was taken of SCP-811 just
staring at the camera, the resulting photo

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:08.470
depicted a human woman with the same height,
build, and facial features as SCP-811, braiding

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:12.360
yellow ribbons into her hair and wearing a
blue sundress.

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:16.840
The attending researchers felt this raised
an interesting question: Were they looking

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:22.760
at an aspiration towards humanity from SCP-811,
or was this a yearning to return to what had

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:24.280
been before?

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:29.220
There was only one way to find out: Conduct
an interview with the creature herself.

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:34.900
When the interview began, the researchers
pressed 811 on some of her earliest memories.

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:39.680
One of the key details she shared was regarding
a mysterious man whom she claimed came to

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:42.650
her before she looked like she did now.

00:11:42.650 --> 00:11:45.220
Back when her skin was soft and pink.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:46.220
The Bad Man.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:51.070
He injected something into her arm, and whatever
it was, it changed her.

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:52.670
Mutated her.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:55.230
Took away her precious humanity.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:59.850
The first thing she remembered feeling after
that was an all-consuming hunger, and then

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:03.490
melting and devouring the one who changed
her.

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:08.920
Destroying any possible answers as to who
he was or why he did it in the process.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:15.070
It was a story of victimization and dehumanization
so cruel and upsetting that Researcher Wachtel,

00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:20.510
an assistant researcher attending the interview,
actually threw up - later debriefing interviews

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:26.390
revealed it was because he had a daughter
of roughly the same age, with long, dark hair.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:31.470
If SCP-811 has any parents herself, we may
never know.

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:37.800
Such is the strange tragedy of SCP-811, whether
you wish to call her by her number, a nickname

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:41.420
like the Swamp Woman, or her self-given name
of Aé.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:46.670
We’ll likely never know who she was before,
as not even she knows now.

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:51.820
It’s an unsettling reminder that all of
our grasps on humanity are looser than you

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:52.820
think.

00:12:52.820 --> 00:12:58.100
Sometimes, all it takes is one chance encounter
to change who you are completely...

00:12:58.100 --> 00:13:04.510
Now go check out “SCP-2845 - Alien God Crash
Lands on Earth - THE DEER” and “Minecraft

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:10.820
World Destroyer SCP-4335 - A Welt In The Crucible”
for more fascinating anomalous creatures!

